# THE DIVE'S LAUNCH DECK — EDIT ME (owner 2026-08-30: "you can just plan it out
# with ascii characters like we've done with the ship builder").
#
# This is the ground a run starts on. It spawns FROZEN at depth 1, like a nest,
# and the game reads the BERTHS straight out of it: every run of empty cells
# wide enough to hold a hull becomes a berth, and a candidate ship is moored
# just below its centre. Move a gap here and the ship moves with it.
#
#   -  platform  — solid to stand on, and S+jump drops you through it
#   .  empty     — a BERTH. A ship hangs under the middle of each one.
#
# SCALE, because it is the thing that keeps biting: the game runs at 8x, so ONE
# CHARACTER HERE IS 128 WORLD PIXELS. The player is 80x144 px — about one cell
# wide and one tall. An on-foot screen is ~6,500 px, so about 50 characters.
# The starter hull is 96 characters wide; the Blueprint Loft test ship is 22.
#
# The layout below, left to right:
#
#   20 platform  |  32 berth (a small hull)  |  20 platform  |  110 berth (the
#   starter)  |  20 platform
#
# You start on the MIDDLE platform, with a berth a step to either side. Walk off
# an edge — or drop through the platform — and you land on the ship below. Walk
# off the FAR END instead and there is nothing under you, which is the run with
# no ship at all.
#
# 'origin COL ROW' names which character is deck cell (0,0).

origin 61 0
